{
 "format": 1,
 "effect": 209,
 "name": "Sorceress spawn",
 "doc": "\"Sorceress\" spawn (enemy attacks 319 / 327 of the time-compression sorceresses c0m115 / c0m116 / c0m117): the battle stage swapped for the next one while the stage, rendered into VRAM (0x240, 0x100), is drawn back as tiles, flashes white and ripples on a screen grid around the caster's head, fading to the new stage's colours; the glow, the 12 bursts, the swirl (timeline A), rising and closing rings at the caster, the screen flash, the sound; the action result at tick 124. Timeline B (the wormlike c0m117) adds screen fades, a camera shake and a voice. Its tasks are the port's code (FFNx mag209_sorceress_spawn.cpp) run on the program's memory (its grid points in the module; its grid cells in the summon data, where the next stage's file is loaded first); its texture is exe data (the setup's TIM), its file loader the engine's bare ret.",
 "copy": {
